  "details": "Apple has guidelines to save files on iOS, and they says files should go to relevant directories. According to the guidelines, I think that the most of the files such as contents caches should go to `Library/Caches`.\n\nBut the iOS client saves many files into Files app (see attached screenshot). Files app should be used only for saving user-created files (for example, downloaded files of web browsers, document files of office apps)\n\nEnvironments\n\n- VRChat beta 2024.2.3(333)\n\n- iOS 17.5.1\n\n- iPhone 14 Pro\n\nDocumentation\n\nFile System Programming Guide:\n\nhttps://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/FileSystemProgrammingGuide/FileSystemOverview/FileSystemOverview.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40010672-CH2-SW1\n\nOptimizing Your App's Data for iCloud Backup:\n\nhttps://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/optimizing_your_app_s_data_for_icloud_backup/",
